+# browserctl MCP
+
+This extension exposes the dedicated `browserctl` session as MCP tools so an
+agent can drive a Chromium window through one stable, serialized control
+surface.
+
+The design is intentionally single-track:
+
+1. Call `ensure_browserctl_session`
+2. Call `browserctl_observe`
+3. Act with `browserctl_click`, `browserctl_click_element`,
+   `browserctl_type`, `browserctl_type_element`, `browserctl_press`,
+   `browserctl_scroll`, or `browserctl_drag`
+4. Observe again and continue
+
+## Why this exists
+
+`browser-control` is good for raw visible-window control. `browserctl` adds a
+dedicated profile, daemonized session management, tab awareness, and CDP page
+inspection while keeping the same "act like a person" model where needed.
+
+## Tools
+
+* `ensure_browserctl_session`
+* `stop_browserctl_session`
+* `browserctl_status`
+* `browserctl_windows`
+* `browserctl_tabs`
+* `browserctl_observe`
+* `browserctl_page`
+* `browserctl_page_screenshot`
+* `browserctl_eval`
+* `browserctl_activate_tab`
+* `browserctl_open`
+* `browserctl_navigate`
+* `browserctl_click`
+* `browserctl_click_element`
+* `browserctl_drag`
+* `browserctl_scroll`
+* `browserctl_type`
+* `browserctl_type_element`
+* `browserctl_wait_selector`
+* `browserctl_press`
+* `browserctl_wait`
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+vpython3 agents/extensions/install.py add browserctl
+```
+
+If you want one short local command from the repo root on Windows, use:
+
+```powershell
+.\browser-agent.cmd up
+.\browser-agent.cmd mcp
+```
+
+## Local checks
+
+```bash
+python tools/browserctl/launcher.py doctor
+python agents/extensions/browserctl/server.py --status
+python agents/extensions/browserctl/server.py --self-test
+python agents/extensions/browserctl/server.py --stop-session
+```
+
+## Notes
+
+* This uses a dedicated profile under `out/browserctl/profile`.
+* It is Windows-focused today because visible window control is Windows-only.
+* This is a browser automation interface, not a stealth or fingerprint-spoofing
+  layer.
